From b106bc8749af587c51f1bf9133e1a76d728eb241 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alberto Ponces <ponces26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Feb 2026 16:53:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rework securize tweak

Major rework of the securize (device identity spoofing) mechanism.

Move security-sensitive prop spoofing to post-boot in phh-on-boot.sh to
avoid breaking device features. Add GSI fingerprint change detection
(persisted to /metadata) to signal PMS for post-upgrade steps. Greatly
expand the list of device/brand/model/manufacturer properties copied from
vendor to system, add USB gadget string updates, and add a
persist.sys.phh.securize property handler toggle.

Also remove the stale ro.adb.secure=0 entries from base.mk and
system.prop -- the AOSP build system sets this based on the build
variant, and the securize tweak handles setting it to 1 at runtime.

Co-authored-by: Christopher A. Williamson <contact@chrisaw.io>
---
 base.mk             |   2 -
 phh-on-boot.sh      |  27 +++++++++++
 phh-prop-handler.sh |  11 +++++
 rw-system.sh        | 114 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------
 system.prop         |   1 -
 vndk.rc             |  14 ++++--
 6 files changed, 118 insertions(+), 51 deletions(-)

